## What this covers, in plain English

**PHP 8.5 OOP Mastery**

"The Software" above means **everything in this repository** — not just the
`.php` files. The lesson READMEs, the challenge briefs, the quizzes and their
answer keys, `COURSE_PHILOSOPHY.md`, the verification harness, the examples,
the reference solutions and the capstone API are all covered by the same terms.

MIT is written in the vocabulary of software. It is being applied here to a
course, deliberately, so that there is exactly one set of rules and nobody has
to work out which file falls under which licence.

| You want to | Allowed? |
|-------------|----------|
| Work through it, alone or with a team | Yes |
| Use the code in a commercial, closed-source product | Yes |
| Teach from it, for money | Yes |
| Translate it, adapt it, rewrite half of it | Yes |
| Build your own paid course on top of it | **Yes** |
| Remove the attribution entirely | No — keep the copyright notice |

The only obligation is the one in the second paragraph above: keep the
copyright notice with substantial portions of the work. That is it.

## Why this permissive

The point of a course is that people take what they learn and use it. A licence
that made a reader think twice before copying a container, a value object or a
test double into their employer's codebase would be working against the thing
it was written for.

The same logic applies to the writing. If somebody can teach this better, or to
an audience I will never reach, or in a language I do not speak — including for
money — that is more people learning it. More power to them.

## Third-party dependencies

Slim, PHP-DI, PHPUnit and their transitive dependencies are installed by
Composer into `vendor/`, which is not part of this repository. Each carries its
own licence.

The companion course, **Advanced Domain Architecture & Tactical DDD**, is
licensed identically:
https://github.com/monatemedia/php8.5-domain-architecture
